Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The incremental-placement hand-off: write_verilog names gates g<K> by
Abc_NtkForEachNode order; iterating the same order here (immediately
after write_verilog, same network) yields an exact instance<->coordinate
map for the freshly written netlist. Unlocated nodes inherit the last
located coordinate in topological order. Motivation, measured: repeater
chains at interpolated coordinates were SCATTERED by a fresh
global placement (any placement inside a chain's bbox is
HPWL-equivalent) -- slew violations unchanged; repair-style
passes require their positions to be honored, i.e. legalize-only
placement seeded from these dumps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
